{"id": "9cf7861c-999b-41c0-b796-2d8102ba832f", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T15:30:07.766412", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "2dc25c4a-22f5-47f7-81b5-b20bb6af13e4", "action": null, "tool_name": "end_researcher_turn", "tool_call_id": "call-932318fd-52b9-4a89-8404-df892283a0b4", "tool_call": {"id": "call-932318fd-52b9-4a89-8404-df892283a0b4", "responses_item_id": null, "name": "end_researcher_turn", "arguments": "{\"summary\":\"Inspection done; sketch + assumptions handoff\",\"stage\":\"plan\",\"answer\":\"Inspection reported: /workspace contains only task.json (which itself says \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\"); no TorchOpt, TorchViz, models, or scripts in the workspace; Python 3.12.3 system, torch/torchviz/torchopt not installed, network disabled, 24 CPUs, no GPU. Sketch proposed: compare three artifacts — (Gᵃ) autograd backward graph via torchviz.make_dot, (Gᶠ) full per-step functional graph via torch.fx.symbolic_trace, and (Gᵥ) rendered DOT/PNG — across two arms that differ only in the optimizer update implementation (unfused torch Adam vs torchopt.FusedAdam/MetaAdam), keeping model, seed, input, loss, lr/betas/eps identical. Metrics: |V|, |E|, ops bucketed into OPTIM_INTERNAL/ACTIVATION/LINEAR_ALGEBRA/REDUCTION/VIEW/FUSED_KERNEL, depth, duplicate-subgraph hash signature across per-parameter paths, plus a human-rater rubric (optional). Models: Linear + 2–3 layer MLP + small CNN; fixed seed; single traced step; N=3 trials. Assumptions and uncertainties enumerated in four groups (definitional, methodological, environmental, reporting). Awaiting approval before producing the full design.\",\"evidence\":\"1) ls -la /workspace showed only task.json; 2) find /workspace -type f confirmed only task.json; 3) cat /workspace/task.json showed documents.track.md = \\\"Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required\\\"; 4) python3 -c import tests all three libraries not installed; 5) pip3 list confirmed no torch/graphviz/torchopt; 6) nproc=24, GPU disabled per task spec, network disabled per task spec.\",\"assumptions\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Single-step traces are sufficient to characterize structural difference; deterministic given seed, so N=3 trials reported as mean±stddev for stability.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"Execution, if attempted, would need an environment with torch, torchviz, system graphviz, torchopt, and ideally a GPU; without GPU, fusion collapses to functional fusion via MetaAdam + torch.func.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Workspace is intentionally empty per track.md; the design is the deliverable and does not require execution in this bubblewrap environment.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"TorchOpt's \\\"fused Adam\\\" refers to FusedAdam (CUDA/TRITON-fused update kernel) and/or MetaAdam as a functional op over torch.func; it does NOT alter the autograd backward graph — autograd graph is preserved across both arms.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"\\\"less complex\\\" = lower node/edge/op-count on the chosen graph; \\\"more interpretable\\\" = either a structural proxy (label uniformity, subgraph duplication) or a human-rater rubric documented in the design but not executed.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"\\\"TorchViz output\\\" is being used as a passive tracer of the unfused update — not as a competing implementation. Fair comparison holds model/seed/input/loss/optimizer-config identical and varies only the optimizer update kernel.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"\\\"gradient graph\\\" can be disambiguated into three artifacts (autograd backward graph, full per-step functional graph, rendered DOT/PNG); all three will be measured to avoid a trivial answer.</item>\\n\"}],\"uncertainties\":[{\"item\":{\"item\":{\"item\":\"Whether the runtime will ever host torch/torchviz/torchopt; design is delivered as a method, not an executed result, consistent with track.md.</item>\\n\",\"$text\":\"Whether the human-rater leg of \\\"interpretable\\\" is in-scope or purely structural; design reports structural metrics regardless.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Whether \\\"fused\\\" is meant to apply to backward-graph fusion (torch.compile reduce-overhead style) rather than TorchOpt's optimizer-kernel fusion; design assumes the latter.</item>\\n\"},\"$text\":\"Whether the researcher means (a) autograd backward graph only, (b) full per-step functional graph, or (c) both — these give different answers and the design reports all three.</item>\\n\"}]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-eda34bc9-8e91-463a-9908-f51ee2ace4eb", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 14}
